hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24353","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu al-Muthanna, from Abu Ubayy ibn the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Hajjaj said: from the son of the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: There will be rulers whom things distract and they delay prayer from its time, so pray prayer at its time, then make your prayer with them voluntary."
"24354","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to me, Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from a man of the family of Khalid ibn Urfutah, from another, who said: I was with Salim ibn Ubayd on a journey, and a man sneezed and said: Peace be upon you, so he said: Upon you and upon your mother, then he went on, and said: Perhaps you found it in yourself, he said: I did not want you to mention my mother, he said: I could not but say it, I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and a man sneezed and said: Peace be upon you, so he said: Upon you and upon your mother, then he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every state, or: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and let it be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, Yahya doubted, and let him say: May Allah forgive me and you."
